    {
      "text": "He shall not strive, nor cry, Matt. 12:19. Strive to enter in at the strait gate, Luke 13:24. Jews therefore strove among themselves, John 6:52. scribes that were of the Pharisees’ part arose, and strove, Acts 23:9. man that striveth for the mastery is temperate, 1 Cor. 9:25. striving together for the faith, Philip. 1:27. if a man also strive for masteries, 2 Tim. 2:5. that they strive not about words, 2 Tim. 2:14. servant of the Lord must not strive, 2 Tim. 2:24. not yet resisted unto blood, striving against sin, Heb. 12:4.",
